<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Organization of American States</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Organization of American States (OAS) is a regional organisation of the states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> in 1948 and based in Washington, DC. It promotes democracy, human rights, security and development, and it arranged the ceasefire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/football-war">Football War</a> between El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> and Honduras in 1969. It suspended Honduras after the coup of 2009 and readmitted it in 2011.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/organization-of-american-states.jpg" alt="Organization of American States" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Organization_of_American_States.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
